  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SER Training Joint Committees</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the context of advancing pillar five of the technical cooperation agreement between Qatar and the International Labour Ogranization (ILO), this project aims to provide the Ministry of Administrative Development, Labour and Social Affairs (MADLSA) with an insight into the existing labour laws, as well as workplace cooperation (e.g. works councils; in-company councils of employees and management representatives) and the social dialogue model in the Netherlands. Hence, it shall promote general knowledge sharing on the Dutch model embodied by the Social and Economic Council (SER), as well as specific expertise on workplace cooperation and conflict mediation.Ultimately, this project is part of the project partners&apos; broader objective to contribute to Qatar&#x2019;s national dispute settlement mechanism, promote workers voices, and strengthen the sustainability of enterprise-level Joint Committees. This project shall also allow MADLSA and the ILO to inform the SER and Dutch businesses on relevant labour reforms.</narrative>
  </description>
